# Observed: 3139 edits across 61 files apply cleanly with 0 conflicts, but the
# rebuild then fails with 621 stale-name errors in 14 files.
#
# History, so the trend is legible: 18081 errors in 52 files originally; 2993 in
# 36 once colliding renames were skipped; 739 in 16 once macro arguments were
# renamed and unrewritable macro references started vetoing the rename; 621 in
# 14 once fields of a class nested in a class template mapped back to their
# pattern. Each step removed a whole cause, and what is left is a single new
# one -- see below. Macros and nested classes are done; this is neither.
REPO=googletest
RULESET=member_snake_case
EXPECT=known_fail
EXPECT_FAIL_PHASE=rebuild
EXPECT_FAIL_REASON="Qualified dependent names. `Helper<T>::member` inside a template is a DependentScopeDeclRefExpr -- a dependent *name*, not a member access on an object -- and only CXXDependentScopeMemberExpr (`x.member`) has cross-TU resolution. So the declaration is renamed and the qualified reference is not: gtest-internal.h's `&(TypeIdHelper<T>::dummy_)` alone is 229 of the 621 errors, and 311 of them are this shape ('is not a member of'). Minimal repro: template <class T> struct Helper { static int dummyValue; }; template <class T> int* get() { return &Helper<T>::dummyValue; }"
